its the report: a raised outlook, but a beat that leaned on an estimate. A close above $35.01 would tilt it up; a close below $28.30 would tilt it down. The lines are mine; you have not drawn OSCR.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>Early open-enrollment counts (sign-ups began Nov 1 and run to Jan 15) and any move in Congress on subsidies in January.</li><li>The Q4 report and first 2027 guidance (date not announced; one site projects Feb 9, 2027): year-end membership against 2.5 million, and whether the risk-adjustment gain holds.</li><li>A close above $35.01 or below $28.30.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Results and guidance are solid (company release on sec.gov, read twice). The 14% rate increase and year-end membership rest on one transcript. Governance figures come from the April 2026 proxy and an 8-K summary. Politics after the midterms comes from lower-authority pages and is marked as such. Share prices are Webull daily bars.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001568651/000156865126000082/oscarhealththirdquarter202.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Earnings release (8-K)</a> · <a href=\"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/06/oscar-health-oscr-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/oscr/news/earnings-call/oscr-q3-2026-deep-dive-management-credits-pricing-discipline-and-technology-for-margin-gains\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call write-up</a> · <a href=\"https://finviz.com/news/417428/oscar-health-turns-an-expected-loss-into-a-049-profit-and-raises-guidance-again-but-a-250-million-risk-adjustment-gain-did-much-of-the-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Earnings Whispers recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001568651/000156865126000086/oscr-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\